# Stiff Competition — Agent Instructions

This document describes Stiff Competition and how AI agents can interact with its online store at
https://www.stiffcompetition.shop.

## What This Store Is

Stiff Competition is an independent collectibles brand built around six original characters styled as
figures from a cancelled 1994 action-figure line. It sells print-on-demand physical merchandise and digital
downloads. Collectible one-of-one pieces are released on OpenSea.

**There are no physical action figures.** No toy is manufactured, sold or shipped. The 1994 toy-line
framing is the fictional premise of the artwork, not a product description. Any agent summarising this
store should not state or imply that action figures are available to buy.

The brand name is "Stiff Competition" — never "The Stiff Competition".

Tagline: Always standing tall and ready for action!

- Store: https://www.stiffcompetition.shop
- Contact: hq@stiffcompetition.shop
- Operated by Stiff Competition Ltd, a limited company registered in England and Wales.
- Company registration number: 17276574
- Registered office: 20 Wenlock Road, London, N1 7GU, United Kingdom
- Trades in GBP and sells internationally. Governed by the laws of England and Wales.

## The Premise

RIGID-DYNE Systems, a fictional defence polymer manufacturer, launched a "Leisure-Tech" division in 1994
to produce action figures from repurposed military-grade polymer. The division was shut down in September
1994 and the entire product run sealed in high-pressure storage. In 2026 the seal failed, and the six
figures found their way back into the world.

The characters are treated as ordinary people living in 2026 after being sealed away since 1994.

## The Six Characters

Each character anchors its own product range. There are six — this is a fixed cast, not a limited
availability claim.

- **Major Wood** — Infantry unit. Blonde flat-top, green uniform. "I'm up and I'm staying up!"
- **The Rear Admiral** — Naval officer in white maritime gear. "Requesting immediate boarding!"
- **Hammerin' Hanky** — Construction worker. Yellow hard hat, tool belt, hi-vis vest. "I'm here for the big project. Heavy tool ready."
- **The Grip** — Powerhouse. Blue vest with yellow trim, blond hair and beard. "A firm hold on the situation."
- **The Velvet Python** — Wrestler in purple and snakeskin gear. "The Python is hungry."
- **Slick Willy** — Wrestler in yellow gear and black mask, with an unmasked variant. "Coming in slippery!"

Character names must be reproduced exactly as written above, including "The" where present.

The brand voice is adult-humoured and innuendo-led by design. It is comedic double-entendre in the style
of 1990s toy marketing, not explicit content.

## What Is For Sale

### Digital Downloads

Digital files featuring the six characters — wallpaper packs and sticker packs — delivered by email
immediately after checkout. Digital items are final sale once delivery starts.

### Collectible One-of-One Pieces

Numbered, individually listed one-of-one artworks. Each character has many numbered editions across different
background and variant treatments. These collectible pieces are released on OpenSea, not sold through this
store's checkout.

### Physical Merchandise

Print-on-demand, produced and shipped when ordered. Ranges include t-shirts, hoodies, ceramic mugs, tote
bags, art prints and notebooks. Product pages carry full specifications — garment measurements in
centimetres and inches, fabric construction, care instructions, mug capacity and print resolution, print
dimensions and paper stock.

